//  M.A.U.S. UTILITY UNIT -- FLYER PLACEHOLDER BODY VARIANT
//
//  Sibling of drone/body/drone_placeholder.monsterpart. Read that file's header
//  for how category + type binding works; only what DIFFERS is recorded here.
//
//  WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE AND A SEPARATE FOLDER
//
//  "category" is the binding key for a monstertype's part pool. The engine
//  gathers every monsterpart whose category matches an entry in the
//  monstertype's "categories" and picks one at random. A flyer sharing
//  "petports_drone" would randomly wear the ground unit's body -- and the
//  ground unit would randomly wear this one. So the flyer carries its own
//  category, which means its own monsterpart, which means its own pngs.
//
//  THE ART
//
//  body_0_lit.png is byte-identical to the drone's. Only the glow layer differs:
//  the flyer's fullbright is the drone's pink rotated to hue 223 with saturation
//  and value held, which keeps each of the three colours within ~0.02 luminance
//  of its pink original so the sprite's internal contrast survives the recolor.
//
//  Pink versus blue also survives red-green colour blindness, which matters for
//  the same reason the treat palette does: blue is the one channel deuteranopia
//  and protanopia both preserve. A red/green pair for two unit classes would
//  have been the wrong choice here.
//
//  NAME. Still "placeholder" for the same reason the drone's is: renaming is
//  free while there is exactly one variant per category and expensive once
//  there are several, since which monsterpart a unit wears follows from its
//  seed over the matching set.

{
  "name" : "flyer_placeholder",
  "category" : "petports_flyer",
  "type" : "body",

  "frames" : {
    "body" : "body_0_lit.png",
    "bodyfullbright" : "body_0_fullbright.png"
  }
}
